- id: certified_mail_letter
  name: Certified Mail Letter to Landlord
  description: A written request for repairs sent to the landlord via certified mail,
    serving as proof of notice before filing an HP action.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id004 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-control/
    - https://housingcourtanswers.org/answers/for-tenants/hp-actions-tenants/
    sample_quotes:
    - Write a letter to the landlord List the repairs and services you need Send by
      certified mail
    - the tenant must write a letter to the landlord, mailed by certified mail, describing
      the problem
    suggested_aliases: *id004
- id: certified_mail_notices
  name: Certified Mail Notices
  description: Proof of sending complaints or notices to the landlord via certified
    mail, often required to establish notice of defects.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id005 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/10582208/304-306-e-83-realty-llc-v-mason/
    sample_quotes:
    - Tenant sent a certified letter to the landlord detailing the mold issue, which
      was entered as evidence.
    suggested_aliases: *id005
- id: certified_mail_receipt
  name: Certified Mail Receipt
  description: Proof of mailing via certified mail, return receipt requested, for
    notice of surrender of possession.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id006 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/if-you-want-to-break-your-lease/
    sample_quotes:
    - Send notice by certified mail, return receipt requested, and keep the proof
      of mailing for your records.
    suggested_aliases: *id006
