  description: Property ownership records from the NYC Department of Finance's Automated
    City Register Information System (ACRIS), used to identify the landlord.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id075 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://housingcourtanswers.org/answers/for-tenants/hp-actions-tenants/
    sample_quotes:
    - The Department of Finance’s ACRIS website also has property records.
    suggested_aliases: *id075
- id: public_assistance_breakdown
  name: Public Assistance Breakdown
  description: A detailed statement from public assistance showing benefits or payments,
    used as evidence.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id077 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://housingcourtanswers.org/answers/for-tenants/stop-an-eviction/
    sample_quotes:
    - What is good evidence? documents money orders applications receipts commitment
      letters breakdown from public assistance
    suggested_aliases: *id077
- id: public_assistance_case_documents
  name: Public Assistance Case Documents
  description: Documents showing an open public assistance case with full cash assistance
    for FHEPS eligibility.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id078 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://housingcourtanswers.org/answers/for-tenants/housing-court-tenants/rent-arrears-tenants/
    sample_quotes:
    - You must have an open public assistance case with full cash assistance and children
      under 18 years old living in the apartment.
    suggested_aliases: *id078
- id: public_assistance_docs
  name: Public Assistance Documents
  description: Papers from public assistance, Section 8, or other rental assistance
    programs that help pay rent, used as evidence.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id079 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://housingcourtanswers.org/answers/for-tenants/housing-court-tenants/tenant-nonpayment-cases/
    sample_quotes:
    - Find papers from public assistance, Section 8 or other program that is helping
      you pay...
    suggested_aliases: *id079
- id: ra_89c_form
  name: RA-89C Form
  description: A form used by rent-controlled tenants to file an overcharge complaint
    with DHCR.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id080 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-control/
    sample_quotes:
    - rent controlled tenants can file and overcharge complaint with DHCR using the
      form RA-89C
    suggested_aliases: *id080
- id: ra_94_form
  name: RA-94 Form
  description: A form filed by a rent-controlled tenant to challenge a rent increase,
    serving as evidence of the challenge.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id081 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-control/
    sample_quotes:
    - To challenge the increase, you must file an RA-94 within 35 days of receiving
      the RN-26
    suggested_aliases: *id081
- id: rn_26_notice
  name: RN-26 Notice
  description: A notice from the landlord to the tenant regarding a rent increase
    application, used as evidence to challenge the increase.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id082 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/rent-control/
    sample_quotes:
    - To challenge the increase, you must file an RA-94 within 35 days of receiving
      the RN-26
    suggested_aliases: *id082
- id: receipts
  name: Receipts
  description: Receipts as evidence of payments or transactions, useful in tenant
    defenses.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id083 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://housingcourtanswers.org/answers/for-tenants/stop-an-eviction/
    sample_quotes:
    - What is good evidence? documents money orders applications receipts commitment
      letters breakdown from public assistance
    suggested_aliases: *id083
- id: record_of_willful_act_or_negligence
  name: Record of Willful Act or Negligence
  description: Evidence of a tenant's willful act, gross negligence, neglect, or abuse
    causing a violation.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id084 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://nycadmincode.readthedocs.io/t27/c02/sch02/art01/
    sample_quotes:
    - caused by his or her own wilful act... or the result of such tenant's gross
      negligence, neglect or abuse
    suggested_aliases: *id084
- id: relocation_payment_schedule
  name: Relocation Payment Schedule
  description: The official schedule of payments for relocation, including maximum
    or minimum amounts, approved by the mayor.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id086 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://nycadmincode.readthedocs.io/t26/c02/index.html
    sample_quotes:
    - to fix and promulgate and from time to time amend a schedule of payments to
      be made to or for the benefit of and to aid in the relocation of tenants
    suggested_aliases: *id086
- id: rent_breakdown_from_landlord
  name: Rent Breakdown from Landlord
  description: A breakdown from the landlord showing the months and amount of rent
    you owe.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id089 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://housingcourtanswers.org/answers/for-tenants/housing-court-tenants/rent-arrears-tenants/
    sample_quotes:
    - Breakdown from the landlord showing the months and amount of rent you owe
    suggested_aliases: *id089
- id: rgb_guidelines
  name: Rent Guidelines Board Increases
  description: Official RGB annual adjustment rates for rent-stabilized lease renewals,
    used to verify lawful increases.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id090 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.metcouncilonhousing.org/help-answers/about-rent-stabilization/
    sample_quotes:
    - for a one-year renewal there is a 3% increase, or for a two-year renewal there
      is a 4.5% increase
    suggested_aliases: *id090
- id: rent_history
  name: Rent History
  description: A record of a tenant's rent history, which can be used to verify rent
    stabilization status and support claims.
  jurisdiction: NYC
  status: proposed
  aliases: &id091 []
  _bootstrap:
    sources:
    - https://www.justfix.org/en/learn/air-conditioning-laws
    sample_quotes:
    - Get your apartment's Rent History
    suggested_aliases: *id091
